Description: the NextBSD ABI, NextBSD:<major>:<arch>
 NextBSD's own packages carry the ABI NextBSD:27:<arch> (amd64, aarch64) for
 NextBSD 27.0.0. Its base is built from FreeBSD's sources, so /usr/bin/uname
 and /bin/sh carry FreeBSD's ELF ABI note (name "FreeBSD",
 NT_FREEBSD_ABI_TAG, desc __FreeBSD_version), and upstream pkg would compute
 FreeBSD:<__FreeBSD_version major>:<arch>. NextBSD may keep
 __FreeBSD_version at the releng/15.1 API level (1501000) or move it to
 2700000; the ABI must be NextBSD:27 either way.
 .
 A new OS, PKG_OS_NEXTBSD, named "NextBSD": major-version-only ABI strings,
 amd64 spelled "amd64", so ABI NextBSD:27:amd64 and ALTABI (lower-cased
 legacy form) nextbsd:27:x86:64. pkg_os_is_freebsd_like() in pkg_abi.h names
 the places where NextBSD is handled as FreeBSD: the osversion format
 (OSVERSION, the FreeBSD_version annotation pkg create stamps, the
 newer-osversion check, ABI= requiring OSVERSION), ELF and shlib analysis
 (provides/requires, Linux and 32-bit compat flags) and the pkgbase shlib
 ABI rule in the solver.
 .
 Detection: when the ABI comes from the ABI file (no ABI set in the
 environment, with -o or in pkg.conf) and its ELF note says FreeBSD, the ABI
 is NextBSD's if the running system is NextBSD: kern.ostype (uname -s) is
 "NextBSD", or uname(3) says so. The version comes from the NextBSD release,
 kern.osrelease (uname -r) "27.0.0", not from the note or kern.osreldate:
 major 27, OSVERSION <major> * 100000 + <minor> * 1000 = 2700000. On
 NextBSD, ELF objects with FreeBSD's note are native objects for shlib
 analysis. ${ABI}, ${ALTABI}, ${OSNAME}, ${RELEASE}, ${VERSION_MAJOR} and
 ${OSVERSION} in pkg.conf and repository files, pkg config ABI and pkg -vv
 follow.
 .
 Package matching is unchanged: a package's abi must match the computed ABI,
 so NextBSD accepts NextBSD:27:<arch> packages. An explicit
 ABI=FreeBSD:15:<arch> (with OSVERSION, or IGNORE_OSVERSION=yes) never goes
 through the detection and works exactly as before, so a user can still
 select FreeBSD packages.
 .
 OSMAJOR is __FreeBSD__, the toolchain triple's FreeBSD major (15), and no
 NextBSD release. pkg is part of NextBSD's base and is upgraded with it from
 the NextBSD repository, so for a NextBSD ABI the "Major OS version upgrade
 detected" check does not apply and is skipped. A FreeBSD:15 override still
 compares against OSMAJOR.
Origin: NextBSD
Bug: https://github.com/nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel/issues/376
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-31
